heck. Point 14 says all smart people are furry. So since Erin is smart, she is furry.\n\nPoint 15: Furry people are cold. Erin is cold, and she's furry, so that checks out.\n\nSo Erin is smart, furry, cold, white, and blue. Now, does being smart and furry make her round? Yes, according to point 16. So smart and furry people are round. Since Erin is both, she must be round.\n\nWait, but earlier I thought that being blue doesn't necessarily mean she's round. But now, through point 16, since she's smart and furry, she's round. So Erin is round.\n\nTherefore, the statement \"Erin is not round\" would be false because Erin is round.\n\nWait, but let me double-check. Is there any possibility that Erin isn't round? Let me see. The only way Erin wouldn't be round is if she's not smart or not furry. But Erin is smart (point 5) and since all smart people are furry (point 14), she's furry. So she's smart and furry, making her round (point 16). So yes, Erin is round.\n\nTherefore, the statement \"Erin is not round\" is false.\n</think>\n\nThe statement \"Erin is not round\" is false because Erin is round based on the given information.\n\n**Answer: B) False**",
