ent is false. But let me make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nLet me retrace:\n\n- Lion is rough (11).\n- All rough people are nice (4). So lion is nice.\n- All nice people are cold (7). So lion is cold.\n\nTherefore, the lion is cold. So the statement \"The lion is not cold\" is false.\n\nBut wait, let me check if there's any other angle. Maybe the lion's color or other attributes affect this.\n\nThe lion is green (10). There's a rule that if someone sees the lion, they are green (5). But that's about others, not the lion itself. So the lion's color is green, but that doesn't directly relate to coldness.\n\nAlso, the lion sees the cat (12). The cat is both green and red (3 and 4). The cat likes the lion (5). The dog chases the cat (6), and the dog is red (7). The dog sees the bald eagle (8) and the lion (9). The bald eagle chases the cat (1) and likes the dog (2). \n\nThere's also a rule that if someone chases the dog and the dog likes the cat, then they see the bald eagle (8). So, the bald eagle chases the cat, which is red and green. The dog chases the cat, and the dog is red. The dog sees the bald eagle and the lion. The lion is green and rough.\n\nWait, but the key point is that the lion is rough, which makes it nice, which makes it cold. So the lion is cold. Therefore, the statement that the lion is not cold is false.\n</think>\n\nThe lion is cold because being rough makes it nice, and all nice people are cold. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\nB) False",
