squirrel. The squirrel is big, so the squirrel needs the squirrel. Therefore, the statement is false because the squirrel does need the squirrel.\n\nYes, that makes sense. So, the answer should be B) False.\n</think>\n\nThe statement \"The squirrel does not need the squirrel\" is false because the squirrel, being big, needs the squirrel according to the given implications.\n\n**Answer: B) False**",
