point 15), so Fiona is big.\n\nNow, the statement is whether Fiona is not big. Since Fiona is big, the statement \"Fiona is not big\" is false.\n\nWait, but let me make sure I didn't miss any other information that could affect this. For example, point 19: If Anne is nice, then Anne is cold. Anne is nice (point 1), so Anne is cold (point 4). Also, Anne is young (point 3), and point 18: If someone is young and white, then they are cold. Anne is young and white, so she's cold, which matches.\n\nPoint 20: Big, young people are nice. Anne is young and, from point 2, she's white. But point 20 says big, young people are nice. Wait, Anne is young, but she's not necessarily big. Wait, point 21: Big people are young. So Anne is young, and if she's big, she's nice. But Anne is not said to be big, only that she's nice, white, and young.\n\nWait, but Fiona is kind, and kind people are big, so Fiona is big. So the statement \"Fiona is not big\" is false because she is big.\n\nI think that's the conclusion. So the answer should be B) False.\n</think>\n\nThe statement \"Fiona is not big\" is false because Fiona is kind, and kind people are big.\n\n**Answer: B) False**",
