t 14: Kind things are blue. So, since Dave is kind, he's blue.\n\nFrom statement 13: White, blue things are furry. So, since Dave is white and blue, he's furry.\n\nTherefore, Dave is furry. So, the statement \"Dave is not furry\" is false.\n\nWait, but let me check if there's any other way. Let me see if there's any contradiction or if I missed something.\n\nWait, from statement 15: All green things are furry. So, if something is green, it's furry. But Dave is not green, he's white. So, that doesn't apply.\n\nBut from statement 14, kind things are blue, so Dave is blue. From statement 13, white, blue things are furry, so Dave is furry.\n\nTherefore, the statement is false because Dave is furry.\n</think>\n\nThe statement \"Dave is not furry\" is false because based on the given information, Dave is both kind and white. From the context, kind things are blue (statement 14), so Dave is blue. Additionally, white, blue things are furry (statement 13), making Dave furry. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\n**Answer: B) False**",
